From 9fc12d077ad1afc70af7c3449b63455cf48ec4c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:51:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/40] board: samsung: exynos-mobile: the boot menu of the
 Galaxy S10+

The phone has no serial port that a user can reach: the connector carries
it, but only behind a jig that this port could not make work, and the one
thing a user does have is the panel and three keys.  So the boot loader
gets a menu on the panel, driven by volume up, volume down and power.

Eight entries, and each one does something a person with a phone in their
hand actually needs: continue, fastboot, the UEFI maintenance menu, reboot,
power off, a storage report, the driver model tree and download mode.  The
two diagnostic entries are there because this is a port under construction
and the answers they print are otherwise unreachable without a cable.

Four languages, because the point of the panel is that it is the only thing
the user can read.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
