  * mode one: it shows a picture when it is triggered, and by the time a boot
- * loader runs nothing is triggering it any more, so whatever is written to the
- * framebuffer stays invisible and the screen keeps the picture it came up
- * with.  The register is this SoC's DECON_HW_SW_TRIG_CONTROL, and the address
- * of the controller comes out of the device tree, so nothing at all happens on
- * a board whose tree has no such controller.  The value written to it is the
- * one uniLoader hands the sibling phone of this family.
- *
- * UNVERIFIED: none of this has been tried on hardware.
+ * loader runs nothing is triggering it any more, so whatever is written to
+ * the framebuffer stays invisible and the screen keeps the picture it came up
+ * with.  That is why the trigger is handed over again after every band and
+ * not just once.  The controller's address comes out of the device tree, so
+ * nothing at all happens on a board whose tree has no such controller; the
+ * register offset and the value are constants, and the value is the one
+ * uniLoader hands the sibling phone of this family.
